74
00:05:01,140 --> 00:05:02,880
Come back, Poxo!

75
00:05:03,140 --> 00:05:04,800
Hey, you okay out here?

76
00:05:05,100 --> 00:05:09,940
I got to experience so many new things
since we went on that expedition.

77
00:05:10,240 --> 00:05:12,420
That alone made it all worth it.

78
00:05:13,220 --> 00:05:14,050
Hello there.

79
00:05:14,560 --> 00:05:15,740
You know what?

80
00:05:16,460 --> 00:05:18,800
Right now, I'm so grateful.

81
00:05:19,840 --> 00:05:24,016
Even though half the village was
destroyed, everything turned out A-OK.

82
00:05:24,300 --> 00:05:25,760
And that's not all.

83
00:05:25,980 --> 00:05:28,537
I'm relieved that you
found your place here.

84
00:05:28,620 --> 00:05:31,240
Did you see how long that line was?

85
00:05:31,980 --> 00:05:34,400
I was afraid they wouldn't like you.

86
00:05:34,760 --> 00:05:38,940
But then, before I knew it, you
became friends with everybody. Yay!

87
00:05:39,600 --> 00:05:41,840
So, I was worried for nothing.

88
00:05:42,080 --> 00:05:43,180
I'm so happy.

89
00:05:46,940 --> 00:05:49,160
She was worried about my well-being?

90
00:05:49,580 --> 00:05:51,420
She really is a good person.

91
00:05:53,160 --> 00:05:54,620
Sleep well, Lamas.

92
00:05:55,220 --> 00:05:56,338
Here's to tomorrow.

93
00:05:58,840 --> 00:06:03,016
The merchants are always busy in the
morning getting their shops ready.

94
00:06:03,420 --> 00:06:07,637
As expected, there are lots of carpenters
as well as hunters on guard duty.

95
00:06:07,720 --> 00:06:09,661
And everyone's got to eat, right?

96
00:06:09,980 --> 00:06:12,156
Director Bear sent summons for Lamas.

97
00:06:12,280 --> 00:06:16,868
I'm not sure why, but I hope it's to
reward her for the successful expedition.

98
00:06:17,920 --> 00:06:19,360
Good news, Boxo!

99
00:06:19,580 --> 00:06:23,097
The director asked me to personally
help out with a special request!

100
00:06:23,180 --> 00:06:24,077
Isn't that great?

101
00:06:24,160 --> 00:06:25,520
Hello there! Uh-huh!

102
00:06:25,700 --> 00:06:27,637
I'll be cleaning up rumble around town!

103
00:06:27,720 --> 00:06:29,500
I should have guessed.

104
00:06:31,540 --> 00:06:32,370
Munami!

105
00:06:32,453 --> 00:06:33,283
Missus!

106
00:06:33,366 --> 00:06:34,257
I'm here to help you out.

107
00:06:34,340 --> 00:06:36,457
Your blessing is gonna
come in handy for sure.

108
00:06:36,540 --> 00:06:38,246
We'll be relying on you then.

109
00:06:39,440 --> 00:06:40,280
Hello there.

110
00:06:41,060 --> 00:06:42,837
Is this where we were assigned?

111
00:06:42,920 --> 00:06:45,237
Oh, there's the box with
the mind of its own.

112
00:06:45,320 --> 00:06:46,840
That's great. Lucky us.

113
00:06:46,940 --> 00:06:47,957
And the pay is good.

114
00:06:48,040 --> 00:06:49,981
We'll buy a whole bunch of stuff.

115
00:06:54,460 --> 00:06:55,720
The cart's all full.

116
00:06:55,880 --> 00:06:56,998
I'll be right back.

117
00:06:59,920 --> 00:07:01,332
Because of her blessing,

118
00:07:01,420 --> 00:07:03,657
Lamas gained a reputation
of being a screw-up,

119
00:07:03,740 --> 00:07:06,681
so her fellow hunters
treated her like a nuisance.

120
00:07:06,820 --> 00:07:09,277
Perhaps if she'd been
given more jobs like this,

121
00:07:09,360 --> 00:07:11,637
they would have seen the
upsides of her blessing.

122
00:07:11,720 --> 00:07:13,040
There you are, Lamas.

123
00:07:13,220 --> 00:07:14,897
Looks like you're hard at work, huh?

124
00:07:14,980 --> 00:07:19,117
I figured you youngsters might be hungry
after looking around all this junk.

125
00:07:19,200 --> 00:07:21,057
Choose whatever you'd like from Boxo.

126
00:07:21,140 --> 00:07:21,970
It's on me.

127
00:07:22,520 --> 00:07:25,097
Oh, naturally that goes
for you ladies as well.

128
00:07:25,180 --> 00:07:28,517
Well, if you're fine, then I'll have
one of these and one of those, too!

129
00:07:28,600 --> 00:07:32,277
Remember, Lamy, at times like this, you
should pick the most expensive things.

130
00:07:32,360 --> 00:07:35,817
Since you so generously offered, why
don't we start with a hundred soups?

131
00:07:35,900 --> 00:07:37,724
Wait, let's be reasonable here.

132
00:07:39,120 --> 00:07:42,357
The truth is, I wanted to ask
if you would join our party.

133
00:07:42,440 --> 00:07:43,270
Hmm?

134
00:07:43,353 --> 00:07:45,260
That goes for Boxo, too, of course.

135
00:07:45,640 --> 00:07:47,052
Nope, thank you, though.

136
00:07:48,040 --> 00:07:48,870
Okay, then.

137
00:07:49,640 --> 00:07:51,237
Why in the world would you say no?

138
00:07:51,320 --> 00:07:53,717
That was an invitation to
join the Menagerie of Fools!

139
00:07:53,800 --> 00:07:57,077
Because we need all the help we
can get rebuilding the village.

140
00:07:57,160 --> 00:08:00,336
I can't run off like that
before the repairs are done.

141
00:08:02,920 --> 00:08:03,940
Would you be Mr.

142
00:08:04,060 --> 00:08:06,957
Boxo, the strange magic
artifact with a mind of its own?

143
00:08:07,040 --> 00:08:07,870
Hello there.

144
00:08:08,180 --> 00:08:10,977
I suppose that phrase is
your way of saying yes.

145
00:08:11,060 --> 00:08:12,940
Hey, Boxo, I'm back now.

146
00:08:13,100 --> 00:08:16,280
Oh, sorry, I didn't mean to
interrupt you. It's fine.

147
00:08:16,580 --> 00:08:18,600
I'm Mokoe from the Exchange House.

148
00:08:19,120 --> 00:08:20,591
This man is my assistant.

149
00:08:20,820 --> 00:08:21,840
His name's Gokai.

150
00:08:22,040 --> 00:08:23,717
It's a pleasure to meet the two of you.

151
00:08:23,800 --> 00:08:24,880
Truth is,

152
00:08:25,080 --> 00:08:28,257
we received word that this stratum
was running low on silver coins,

153
00:08:28,340 --> 00:08:30,458
so we came to investigate the cause.

154
00:08:30,800 --> 00:08:33,682
Seems someone out there
is hoarding silver coins.

155
00:08:33,780 --> 00:08:34,610
Disgraceful.

156
00:08:34,740 --> 00:08:38,020
Oh, that's because everyone
pays Boxo in silver!

157
00:08:38,360 --> 00:08:39,820
Don't tell them that!

158
00:08:40,020 --> 00:08:41,432
That's what I suspected.

159
00:08:41,660 --> 00:08:44,417
Since that's the case, I
have a proposal for you.

160
00:08:44,500 --> 00:08:47,337
We've brought along nearly a
hundred gold coins with us.

161
00:08:47,420 --> 00:08:50,417
Would you mind exchanging
them for your silver coins?

162
00:08:50,500 --> 00:08:51,330
Gold coins?

163
00:08:51,760 --> 00:08:54,637
If I remember right, each
is worth a hundred silver.

164
00:08:54,720 --> 00:08:57,617
When you convert it to yen, I'd
say it's about a hundred thousand.

165
00:08:57,700 --> 00:08:58,994
That's a ton of money.

166
00:08:59,460 --> 00:09:01,120
What do you say? Too bad.

167
00:09:01,440 --> 00:09:03,717
Are you saying you don't accept the offer?

168
00:09:03,800 --> 00:09:05,817
It's not that I don't want to do it,

169
00:09:05,900 --> 00:09:08,777
but I don't have any way of
exchanging currencies right now.

170
00:09:08,860 --> 00:09:13,566
Ooh, maybe if you buy something with a
gold coin, you can get silver's exchange.

171
00:09:14,760 --> 00:09:15,590
Ho, ho, ho!

172
00:09:16,000 --> 00:09:18,471
This is the first gold coin I've accepted.

173
00:09:22,880 --> 00:09:24,897
I think this may actually work out.

174
00:09:24,980 --> 00:09:26,686
Let's keep buying more items.

175
00:09:27,260 --> 00:09:30,377
Finally, I got put through the
damn ringer thanks to that jerk.

176
00:09:30,460 --> 00:09:33,137
If we continue on, we might
start to interfere with Mr.

177
00:09:33,220 --> 00:09:34,177
Boxer's business.

178
00:09:34,260 --> 00:09:35,495
Let's stop for today.

179
00:09:40,540 --> 00:09:43,957
We still have more coins, but
we'll exchange them next time.

180
00:09:44,040 --> 00:09:45,997
I look forward to working with you again.

181
00:09:46,080 --> 00:09:46,910
Amazing.

182
00:09:46,993 --> 00:09:48,757
You gotta be the richest
box thingy in town.

183
00:09:48,840 --> 00:09:51,193
You better be careful to not get robbed.

184
00:09:51,320 --> 00:09:52,200
Hello there.

185
00:09:55,680 --> 00:09:57,500
You could even win a reward.

186
00:09:57,720 --> 00:09:58,980
Yeah, come on.

187
00:09:59,320 --> 00:10:00,400
Come to papa.

188
00:10:02,100 --> 00:10:03,900
Seven. Seven.

189
00:10:05,000 --> 00:10:05,830
Six.

190
00:10:06,020 --> 00:10:07,860
Ah, so close.

191
00:10:09,020 --> 00:10:09,850
Too bad.

192
00:10:10,400 --> 00:10:11,397
It took a while,

193
00:10:11,480 --> 00:10:15,697
but I'm finally able to use this
particular phrase for its intended purpose.

194
00:10:15,780 --> 00:10:18,120
I added the digital lottery function.

195
00:10:18,300 --> 00:10:21,497
Ever since I installed it,
I've increased sales by 30%.

196
00:10:21,580 --> 00:10:22,740
Gotta relax.

197
00:10:23,040 --> 00:10:24,000
Just calm down.

198
00:10:24,220 --> 00:10:26,279
This will be the last one, I swear.

199
00:10:26,460 --> 00:10:28,989
No matter what, I'm
bound to win something.

200
00:10:29,100 --> 00:10:30,320
I can feel it.

201
00:10:30,420 --> 00:10:33,557
I'd even wager this old life
of mine on this final shot.

202
00:10:33,640 --> 00:10:37,228
What the heck are you going on
about this time, you old fool?

203
00:10:37,440 --> 00:10:40,340
That bad habit of yours
is rearing its ugly head.

204
00:10:40,780 --> 00:10:43,857
Knowing you, I bet you don't
remember what day today is.

205
00:10:43,940 --> 00:10:46,840
Of course I do. I remember. I promise.

206
00:10:47,660 --> 00:10:48,800
Sorry, Boxo.

207
00:10:49,200 --> 00:10:52,477
I sent a letter to Hulemy,
but she hasn't responded yet.

208
00:10:52,560 --> 00:10:55,197
She's probably wandering
around a stratum somewhere.

209
00:10:55,280 --> 00:10:58,460
So, could you keep waiting
here for a little longer?

210
00:10:58,840 --> 00:10:59,720
Hello there.

211
00:10:59,900 --> 00:11:02,380
Are you too busy right now? Director!

212
00:11:02,660 --> 00:11:04,337
I'd like to have a chat with you.

213
00:11:04,420 --> 00:11:06,714
Could you visit the Hunter Association?

214
00:11:08,240 --> 00:11:10,097
I mentioned this to you before.

215
00:11:10,180 --> 00:11:12,886
You both performed well
during the expedition.

216
00:11:13,440 --> 00:11:14,677
Without your quick thinking,

217
00:11:14,760 --> 00:11:18,377
there's a high probability the situation
would have gone from bad to worse.

218
00:11:18,460 --> 00:11:19,300
I'm grateful.

219
00:11:20,240 --> 00:11:24,820
By the way, I have a small
favor I'd like to ask you, Boxo.

220
00:11:25,060 --> 00:11:28,040
So, would you mind giving
us a bit of privacy?

221
00:11:29,560 --> 00:11:30,390
All right.

222
00:11:30,473 --> 00:11:32,657
I suppose I'll just wait downstairs, then.

223
00:11:32,740 --> 00:11:33,570
Thank you.

224
00:11:33,653 --> 00:11:36,257
I'll send for you as soon
as our business is done.

225
00:11:36,340 --> 00:11:37,170
Okay.

226
00:11:40,180 --> 00:11:44,177
Recently, a large number of people have
been hoping to migrate to the village.

227
00:11:44,260 --> 00:11:47,297
But increasing the population
brings a number of issues.

228
00:11:47,380 --> 00:11:51,057
One of which is food, but you
can help alleviate any shortages.

229
00:11:51,140 --> 00:11:53,217
That said, there are other concerns.

230
00:11:53,300 --> 00:11:55,397
Hygiene being particularly difficult.

231
00:11:55,480 --> 00:11:58,157
We bear fiends don't
have many physical needs.

232
00:11:58,240 --> 00:12:00,177
Outside of mating season, of course.

233
00:12:00,260 --> 00:12:02,620
It's a shame humans aren't so simple.

234
00:12:03,240 --> 00:12:05,217
They're susceptible to
things like diseases.

235
00:12:05,300 --> 00:12:07,712
which could delay reconstruction efforts.

236
00:12:07,800 --> 00:12:08,680
I see.

237
00:12:09,000 --> 00:12:12,471
This is kind of a sensitive
subject, so he had Lamas leave.

238
00:12:12,620 --> 00:12:15,637
But hey, as a former human
myself, it's just natural.

239
00:12:15,720 --> 00:12:17,779
Why don't you come inside, Shirley?

240
00:12:22,740 --> 00:12:24,020
My name is Shirley.

241
00:12:24,380 --> 00:12:25,792
It's lovely to meet you.

242
00:12:26,580 --> 00:12:28,140
Oh, she's so pretty.

243
00:12:28,860 --> 00:12:32,757
Ideally, allowing more people to live
in the village would be a good thing.

244
00:12:32,840 --> 00:12:34,660
But as the population grows,

245
00:12:34,980 --> 00:12:36,837
we have to tighten health regulations,

246
00:12:36,920 --> 00:12:39,861
which can then create more
problems down the road.

247
00:12:40,180 --> 00:12:42,957
I've got something in mind
for preventing diseases,

248
00:12:43,040 --> 00:12:46,197
but the question is, will
they be able to understand it?

249
00:12:46,280 --> 00:12:48,515
Well, I might as well show it to them.

250
00:12:51,640 --> 00:12:53,057
Oh, how intriguing.

251
00:12:53,140 --> 00:12:56,611
So this is how you go about
changing the products you sell.

252
00:12:58,460 --> 00:13:00,120
What's inside this package?

253
00:13:00,440 --> 00:13:03,377
Is this how you plan to
stop the spread of disease?

254
00:13:03,460 --> 00:13:04,290
Hello there.

255
00:13:04,373 --> 00:13:05,680
Ten silver coins.

256
00:13:05,860 --> 00:13:07,742
It certainly doesn't come cheap.

257
00:13:10,980 --> 00:13:15,357
Looks like there are notches all around
the edges to make opening the bag easier.

258
00:13:15,440 --> 00:13:17,120
How convenient. Hello there.

259
00:13:17,420 --> 00:13:18,420
This material.

260
00:13:18,780 --> 00:13:21,057
I've never seen anything like it before.

261
00:13:21,140 --> 00:13:23,637
It's interesting how it
stretches and contracts.

262
00:13:23,720 --> 00:13:26,237
What's more, there's some
kind of slimy liquid inside.

263
00:13:26,320 --> 00:13:29,677
I'm not doing anything wrong, but
somehow this feels kind of immoral.

264
00:13:29,760 --> 00:13:31,837
How are we supposed to use this thing?

265
00:13:31,920 --> 00:13:34,617
Hold on, it looks like there's
a piece of paper in the box.

266
00:13:34,700 --> 00:13:36,406
Well, let's see what it says.

267
00:13:37,460 --> 00:13:39,260
Ah, so that's how it works.

268
00:13:39,480 --> 00:13:40,937
It's surprisingly simple.

269
00:13:41,020 --> 00:13:43,020
Thank goodness for these diagrams.

270
00:13:43,380 --> 00:13:46,280
This is a truly ingenious
product, Mr. Boxo.

271
00:13:46,480 --> 00:13:48,421
It will protect against diseases.

272
00:13:49,000 --> 00:13:53,353
We should buy them in bulk and hand
them out in the entertainment quarter.

273
00:13:56,020 --> 00:13:57,680
Whew, more happy customers.

274
00:13:58,180 --> 00:13:59,717
Boxo, did something happen?

275
00:13:59,800 --> 00:14:02,153
It feels like you're lighter than usual.

276
00:14:02,760 --> 00:14:06,020
I've got a regular who
comes by in the afternoon.

277
00:14:06,480 --> 00:14:09,833
I've been trying to overlook
her little fits of mischief.

278
00:14:10,940 --> 00:14:12,400
But that ends today!

279
00:14:14,120 --> 00:14:15,480
Please insert coins.

280
00:14:16,680 --> 00:14:17,740
How dare you!

281
00:14:17,980 --> 00:14:20,804
Do you have any idea who
I am, you wretched box?

282
00:14:21,160 --> 00:14:23,700
Bring that thing apart! Listen to me!

283
00:14:23,960 --> 00:14:28,431
Oh, Miss Gracious, Miss Suori's antics
have been getting out of hand lately.

284
00:14:28,780 --> 00:14:31,251
As usual, the little girl showed up again.

285
00:14:32,780 --> 00:14:36,660
Father, you promised me that
you'd come home today. Liar.

286
00:14:41,840 --> 00:14:42,940
Hello there.

287
00:14:45,600 --> 00:14:47,500
You're saying this is for me?

288
00:14:47,900 --> 00:14:49,320
Thank you very much.

289
00:14:52,020 --> 00:14:53,057
Alright then.

290
00:14:53,140 --> 00:14:54,480
Thank you, I guess.

291
00:14:55,040 --> 00:14:57,240
I look forward to serving you again.

292
00:15:02,180 --> 00:15:03,010
Whoa!

293
00:15:03,093 --> 00:15:05,080
I wish I had your figure, Shirley.

294
00:15:05,240 --> 00:15:06,300
I'm so jealous.

295
00:15:07,740 --> 00:15:08,820
You flatter me.

296
00:15:09,620 --> 00:15:13,417
I can't move on my own, so it's not
my fault they decided to put me here.

297
00:15:13,500 --> 00:15:15,912
But boy, am I glad I'm a vending machine.

298
00:15:16,500 --> 00:15:17,330
Boxo!

299
00:15:17,413 --> 00:15:18,594
Could I get the usual?

300
00:15:25,600 --> 00:15:28,477
Thanks, I can't get enough
of this liquid hair soap.

301
00:15:28,560 --> 00:15:31,157
Every time I use it, it makes
my hair feel glossy and clean.

302
00:15:31,240 --> 00:15:33,720
Yep, that's why I've been installed here.

303
00:15:33,940 --> 00:15:37,037
I definitely didn't stock up on these
products just so I'd be brought in.

304
00:15:37,120 --> 00:15:37,950
No Suori.

305
00:15:38,820 --> 00:15:39,650
There's more?

306
00:15:39,960 --> 00:15:41,937
I've been shedding like crazy lately.

307
00:15:42,020 --> 00:15:44,137
Isn't it because your
new coat's growing in?

308
00:15:44,220 --> 00:15:46,457
Yeah, on top of that, I'm aching all over.

309
00:15:46,540 --> 00:15:48,716
Ah, right, it's almost mating season.

310
00:15:49,460 --> 00:15:50,519
Boxo's here today.

311
00:15:50,740 --> 00:15:52,417
Guess I'll stock up on fur wash.

312
00:15:52,500 --> 00:15:53,330
Good idea.

313
00:15:53,600 --> 00:15:55,457
I'll use this to make
my coat look amazing,

314
00:15:55,540 --> 00:15:57,577
and then all the males
will pay attention to me.

315
00:15:57,660 --> 00:16:00,097
Not only that, but it makes
your scent irresistible.

316
00:16:00,180 --> 00:16:02,817
One whiff and my boyfriend
got all hot and bothered,

317
00:16:02,900 --> 00:16:04,677
even though it wasn't mating season.

318
00:16:04,760 --> 00:16:05,590
Seriously?

319
00:16:05,673 --> 00:16:06,894
Only in the bathhouse.

320
00:16:09,500 --> 00:16:14,382
Looks like that hands-on-hip pose is so
universal, they even do it in other worlds.

321
00:16:14,820 --> 00:16:15,650
Ah!

322
00:16:15,733 --> 00:16:16,977
A cold one after a hot bath?

323
00:16:17,060 --> 00:16:18,557
What more can you ask for?

324
00:16:18,640 --> 00:16:19,758
That sounds lovely.

325
00:16:20,000 --> 00:16:21,597
Could I please have one too, Boxo?

326
00:16:21,680 --> 00:16:23,677
I think I'll go with
the brown drink today.

327
00:16:23,760 --> 00:16:26,172
It's got the perfect amount of sweetness.

328
00:16:26,380 --> 00:16:27,210
Sure enough.

329
00:16:27,293 --> 00:16:30,631
After a bath, it's got to be
fruit or coffee-flavored milk.

330
00:16:30,800 --> 00:16:32,557
Straight from the bottle, of course.

331
00:16:32,640 --> 00:16:34,111
It's a bathhouse special.

332
00:16:34,560 --> 00:16:37,400
Hey, Grandpa, what do these numbers mean?

333
00:16:37,560 --> 00:16:39,477
They change whenever you buy something.

334
00:16:39,560 --> 00:16:43,917
If you're lucky and the numbers end up the
same, you can get another item for free.

335
00:16:44,000 --> 00:16:46,357
People say if you're
lucky enough to win here,

336
00:16:46,440 --> 00:16:48,977
then happiness will follow
you for the rest of the day.

337
00:16:49,060 --> 00:16:49,937
That sounds fun!

338
00:16:50,020 --> 00:16:51,057
I want to try, Grandpa!

339
00:16:51,140 --> 00:16:52,757
All right, let's give it a go.

340
00:16:52,840 --> 00:16:55,917
Let's see, why don't we
start you off with a water?

341
00:16:56,000 --> 00:16:57,460
Yeah, that sounds good!

342
00:16:57,680 --> 00:17:00,092
I'm glad I worked up the nerve to return.

343
00:17:00,640 --> 00:17:03,280
And I'm sorry for being
such a bad daughter.

344
00:17:03,520 --> 00:17:04,696
You were right, Mom.

345
00:17:05,120 --> 00:17:06,457
As long as you're safe.

346
00:17:06,540 --> 00:17:07,960
That's all I care about.

347
00:17:08,200 --> 00:17:10,435
I'm happy that you've come home, dear.

348
00:17:12,540 --> 00:17:13,370
Hooray!

349
00:17:13,453 --> 00:17:15,117
I only need one more number to match!

350
00:17:15,200 --> 00:17:16,120
Not so fast.

351
00:17:16,240 --> 00:17:17,557
The last one's the hardest.

352
00:17:17,640 --> 00:17:21,020
Seven! Seven! Seven! Seven!

353
00:17:21,780 --> 00:17:22,960
I got a seven!

354
00:17:23,240 --> 00:17:24,070
I did it!

355
00:17:24,153 --> 00:17:26,280
How come I'm never that lucky?

356
00:17:28,680 --> 00:17:30,677
Hurry up and make your decision, May.

357
00:17:30,760 --> 00:17:33,577
Otherwise, you might run out
of time to get your free item.

358
00:17:33,660 --> 00:17:34,542
Hey, with that!

359
00:17:36,980 --> 00:17:38,677
Here, this is for you, Grandpa.

360
00:17:38,760 --> 00:17:39,590
What's this?

361
00:17:39,673 --> 00:17:41,017
You're giving your prize to me?

362
00:17:41,100 --> 00:17:43,157
My goodness, you don't have to do that.

363
00:17:43,240 --> 00:17:45,340
It's too bad the day's almost over.

364
00:17:45,600 --> 00:17:48,188
It'll only make you
happy for a short while.

365
00:17:48,640 --> 00:17:49,520
How unlucky.

366
00:17:50,320 --> 00:17:51,150
Unlucky?

367
00:17:51,233 --> 00:17:55,880
But, Grandpa, I've been feeling happy
all day because I'm with you and Grandpa.

368
00:17:56,360 --> 00:17:58,419
The rumor about the prize was true.

369
00:18:02,820 --> 00:18:03,820
You're right.

370
00:18:05,520 --> 00:18:08,897
Was it a coincidence that little
May hit the jackpot just now?

371
00:18:08,980 --> 00:18:09,840
It's the best.

372
00:18:10,900 --> 00:18:13,312
Well, some things are better left unsaid.

373
00:18:16,580 --> 00:18:17,410
Boxxo,

374
00:18:17,493 --> 00:18:19,037
I heard that you can use an ability called

375
00:18:19,120 --> 00:18:21,297
mimicry to blend in
with your surroundings.

376
00:18:21,380 --> 00:18:22,260
Is that true?

377
00:18:23,320 --> 00:18:24,150
Hello there!

378
00:18:26,420 --> 00:18:28,177
Wow, that's quite the handy skill.

379
00:18:28,260 --> 00:18:31,677
I bet you could sit right there with it
active and no one would ever notice you.

380
00:18:31,760 --> 00:18:35,757
Now that I've confirmed your ability, I
have a request I'd like to ask of you.

381
00:18:35,840 --> 00:18:36,670
Me?

382
00:18:36,880 --> 00:18:39,157
I'd like you to stake out
the area where a number of

383
00:18:39,240 --> 00:18:42,177
crimes have taken place so you
can identify the perpetrator.

384
00:18:42,260 --> 00:18:46,495
But before we begin the operation,
I'd like to see more of your mimicry.

385
00:18:47,020 --> 00:18:48,260
This spot's perfect.

386
00:18:48,560 --> 00:18:50,777
I've got a clear view of
the Hunters Association.

387
00:18:50,860 --> 00:18:51,690
Not bad.

388
00:18:53,020 --> 00:18:53,850
Boxo!

389
00:18:53,933 --> 00:18:54,900
Where do you go?

390
00:18:55,800 --> 00:18:58,237
Didn't the director say he
was borrowing him for a bit?

391
00:18:58,320 --> 00:18:59,420
Oh, I forgot.

392
00:18:59,880 --> 00:19:01,174
Do you have any plans?

393
00:19:01,280 --> 00:19:02,937
You want to help around here again?

394
00:19:03,020 --> 00:19:05,677
I was going to help out around
the Hunters Association today

395
00:19:05,760 --> 00:19:08,557
so I can meet up with Boxo
whenever he's ready to come back.

396
00:19:08,640 --> 00:19:09,875
All right, all right.

397
00:19:13,400 --> 00:19:14,440
Hello, Lamas.

398
00:19:14,620 --> 00:19:15,677
That's a rare sight.

399
00:19:15,760 --> 00:19:16,697
Boxo isn't with you?

400
00:19:16,780 --> 00:19:17,610
Nope.

401
00:19:17,693 --> 00:19:19,337
Turns out he's helping
out the director today.

402
00:19:19,420 --> 00:19:21,200
Is that so? That's too bad.

403
00:19:22,240 --> 00:19:23,440
He's so popular.

404
00:19:23,700 --> 00:19:24,640
Must be nice.

405
00:19:26,000 --> 00:19:28,240
Ah, what a nice, peaceful day.

406
00:19:28,420 --> 00:19:31,360
Oh, I was looking forward
to some fruit juice.

407
00:19:33,540 --> 00:19:35,560
Boxo's a big, dumb, stupid jerk.

408
00:19:35,740 --> 00:19:37,040
Don't say that, Swari.

409
00:19:37,300 --> 00:19:39,877
If you can't say anything nice,
you shouldn't say it at all.

410
00:19:39,960 --> 00:19:42,780
Look who it is, the booby monster.

411
00:19:43,340 --> 00:19:44,380
Hey, cut it out.

412
00:19:44,540 --> 00:19:46,440
I told you before, it's Lammis.

413
00:19:46,760 --> 00:19:48,000
Whatever, Lammeries.

414
00:19:48,240 --> 00:19:50,257
Have you given any more
thought to my offer?

415
00:19:50,340 --> 00:19:53,780
My name is Lammis, and you
should just give up on that.

416
00:19:53,980 --> 00:19:55,921
I'm never going to give you Boxo.

417
00:19:56,720 --> 00:19:58,417
With the amount I'm offering,

418
00:19:58,500 --> 00:20:00,157
your family could
further it away for three

419
00:20:00,240 --> 00:20:02,517
generations and still
not run out of money.

420
00:20:02,600 --> 00:20:05,977
Like I said, Boxo isn't my
property, so he's not mine to sell.

421
00:20:06,060 --> 00:20:08,717
Besides, money alone would
never be enough to replace him.

422
00:20:08,800 --> 00:20:12,057
You act like you're his friend, but
you want to keep Boxxo all to yourself,

423
00:20:12,140 --> 00:20:12,970
don't you?

424
00:20:13,053 --> 00:20:13,883
Come on, think about it.

425
00:20:13,966 --> 00:20:15,357
Wouldn't he be much
happier spending the rest

426
00:20:15,440 --> 00:20:17,357
of his life with me and
my family's magnificent

427
00:20:17,440 --> 00:20:19,577
residence instead of wasting
his time getting lugged

428
00:20:19,660 --> 00:20:21,937
around by some stumpy
woman with no sex appeal?

429
00:20:22,020 --> 00:20:24,255
I'm a stumpy woman with no sex appeal?

430
00:20:24,440 --> 00:20:27,087
You know, that's rich
coming from you, Suori.

431
00:20:28,340 --> 00:20:29,177
That's not fair.

432
00:20:29,260 --> 00:20:30,460
I'm still growing.

433
00:20:30,700 --> 00:20:32,497
I have plenty to look forward to.

434
00:20:32,580 --> 00:20:35,657
I'll have you know Mother has
even bigger ones than yours.

435
00:20:35,740 --> 00:20:37,397
Oh, no, poor Miss Suori.

436
00:20:37,480 --> 00:20:40,833
She has no idea that the
Madam's been patting her bodies.

437
00:20:40,980 --> 00:20:43,215
Well, we can lay this issue to breast.

438
00:20:43,640 --> 00:20:46,697
Lamouries, can I ask you a
question about something?

439
00:20:46,780 --> 00:20:51,015
I'll think about it, but only if you
start calling me by my actual name.

440
00:20:52,200 --> 00:20:53,030
Ugh.

441
00:20:53,113 --> 00:20:53,943
Fine then, Lamas.

442
00:20:54,026 --> 00:20:55,200
Yes, what is it?

443
00:20:55,800 --> 00:20:56,630
Boxxo.

444
00:20:56,713 --> 00:20:59,020
He's not a simple magic tool, is he?

445
00:20:59,440 --> 00:21:02,205
Tell me, what exactly is
going on inside there?

446
00:21:02,480 --> 00:21:06,892
Well, to tell you the truth, I'm not
really that sure what Boxxo is either.

447
00:21:07,480 --> 00:21:11,237
But he understands what people say, and
he can even respond like he gets it.

448
00:21:11,320 --> 00:21:13,240
To me, he's the same as a human.

449
00:21:13,780 --> 00:21:14,610
I see.

450
00:21:14,780 --> 00:21:16,545
So that's how you think of me.

451
00:21:16,800 --> 00:21:18,000
Thank you, llamas.

452
00:21:19,580 --> 00:21:20,680
I've heard enough.

453
00:21:21,180 --> 00:21:22,837
I'll leave it there for today.

454
00:21:22,920 --> 00:21:25,380
But one day, Boxo will belong to me.

455
00:21:25,880 --> 00:21:29,297
Sooner or later, you'll open your
eyes to the greatness that is Zalori.

456
00:21:29,380 --> 00:21:30,760
Uh-huh, if you say so.

457
00:21:31,280 --> 00:21:32,960
Anyway, Boxo's not here now.

458
00:21:33,100 --> 00:21:34,180
So head back home.

459
00:21:34,680 --> 00:21:36,460
Fine, but I'll be back again.

460
00:21:38,280 --> 00:21:41,097
Until then, I'll let you
continue taking care of him.

461
00:21:41,180 --> 00:21:44,062
Make sure to polish him
up nice and shiny for me.

462
00:21:45,120 --> 00:21:46,737
I don't know if it's just me,

463
00:21:46,820 --> 00:21:50,217
but it seems Suori's been a
lot more talkative than before.

464
00:21:50,300 --> 00:21:51,130
Hello there.

465
00:21:51,920 --> 00:21:53,977
Guaxo, how long have you been there?

466
00:21:54,060 --> 00:21:54,890
What were you doing?

467
00:21:54,973 --> 00:21:56,777
You should have spoken up sooner.

468
00:21:56,860 --> 00:21:59,480
Anyway, all sorts of stuff happened today.

469
00:22:00,040 --> 00:22:02,100
Wanna hear about it? Hello there.

470
00:22:19,680 --> 00:22:20,737
I'll see

471
00:22:20,820 --> 00:22:27,320
you next time

472
00:23:35,240 --> 00:23:36,680
Thank you very much.

473
00:23:37,040 --> 00:23:39,158
I look forward to serving you again.
